rred array's binary operators by their operators (#555's review)\n\nThe walk kept a binary operator's left operand's pointer type for every\noperator, but `p - q` is a ptrdiff_t and `p == q` an int: under a vector\noperator, `(p - q) * h` never tried `h`, and its array was counted short.\nThe walk now goes down both operands of a binary operator, keeping the\nleft one's type, and combines them (check_init_binary_type): a vector\nwhere either operand is one, a pointer for `+` with one pointer or array\noperand and for `-` with a pointer and no pointer, and a scalar for the\nrest, compares of pointers among them. Each token is still read once.\n\nThe fixture \"operators' values in an inferred array\" gains four vectors\npast a difference and compares of pointers (`(l - m) * d`, `(l == m) * d`,\n`(l < m) + d`) and two struct elements through pointer arithmetic of them\n(`*(p + (l - m))`, `p[l == m]`), against clang; on the walk before this\nchange it fails on both paths.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nSigned-off-by: David Gonzalez Martin <davidgmbb@gmail.com>","timestamp":"2026-10-27T11:07:01Z","author":{"name":"David Gonzalez Martin","email":"davidgmbb@gmail.com"},"committer":{"name":"David Gonzalez Martin","email":"davidgmbb@gmail.com"}},"repository":{"id":1421805693,"node_id":"R_kgDOVL8IfQ","name":"buster","full_name":"buster14a/buster","private":false,"owner":{"login":"buster14a","id":139068652,"node_id":"O_kgDOCEoE7A","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/139068652?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/buster14a","html_url":"https://github.com/buster14a","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/buster14a/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/buster14a/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/buster14a/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/buster14a/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/buster14